  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10e-catfishes-from-asia/mystus_bocourti_en/",
      "html": "<p>Due to its extremely prolonged dorsal fin this fascinating species has also been placed in a genus on its own for a long time, namely Heterobagrus. The catfish becomes around 20-25 cm long. It is a very peaceful species; however, fish of small size will be taken as food, but neither congeners nor any other tankmate will be attacked by M. bocourti otherwise.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10e-catfishes-from-asia/mystus_bocourti_en/",
      "html": "<p>Mystus bocourti comes from the river basins of the Mekong and the Chao Phraya in Thailand, Laos, and Cambodia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10e-catfishes-from-asia/mystus_bocourti_en/",
      "html": "<p>The fish feed readily on any usually frozen or live fish food and most often the animals don´t even refuse dried fish food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10e-catfishes-from-asia/mystus_bocourti_en/",
      "html": "<p>Lexicon: Mystus: not known for sure, but most probably derived from the ancient Greek word for “beard”. bocourti: dedication name for F. Bocourt who collected the type specimens. Heterobagrus: means “different Bagrus”; Bagrus is another genus of catfish.</p><p>Suggestion of a common name: Highfin King Cat</p>"
    }
  ],
